## Drum Sing Dance program FAQs

{% faq %}
{% question title="What is the Drum Sing Dance program?" %}
It’s an interactive African music workshop where children drum, sing and dance. Along the way, they also learn about the diverse cultures of West Africa.
{% /question %}

{% question title="How long is each workshop?" %}
Each workshop runs for 30 to 50 minutes. So it fits easily into a morning or afternoon session.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Do we need to supply drums?" %}
No. We bring real African drums and percussion, so every child plays an instrument at no extra cost.
{% /question %}

{% question title="How many workshops are there?" %}
There are five: Groovers in Guinea, Imagination in Mali, Get Down in Ghana, West African Dance Rumble and West African Pop Party.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Do you offer discounts?" %}
Yes. Booking multiple incursions gives you fantastic savings, so you can plan your whole year.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Which areas do you visit?" %}
We visit the Sunshine Coast and Brisbane, as well as services across Australia. What’s more, there are no travel fees.
{% /question %}
{% /faq %}
